{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And this is the thing that you shall do, etc.</b> The intention is that there preceded it the hindering of the action, as I explained (Exodus 27:20), that upon him there is only the command of speech to do them; therefore <b>and this is the thing</b> — this departed from the general implication, and he must perform it, to offer his sacrifices for seven days. And its saying <b>and this</b> is because He preceded and commanded that he clothe Aaron and his sons, and finished by saying <b>and this</b> you shall also do. And if He had not said <b>that you shall do</b> but only ״take a bull,״ etc., there would be room to say that He commands Aaron or his sons to do it; therefore He said ״that you shall do,״ for he is the one who does. And since there is room to say that he was not qualified to offer anything except the offering of the hour, which are the sacrifices of the days of ordination of Aaron and his sons — but an offering that is fixed for all generations, which are the daily offerings of one lamb in the morning and one lamb between the evenings — no; therefore He returned and said <b>and this that you shall do</b>, etc., <b>lambs of the first year, two daily, a continual offering.</b> And lest one understand that he was permitted in the act of continual offerings, therefore He said ״and this,״ to say: he may offer only for the seven days stated in the matter." "And its saying <b>the thing</b> is to be explained according to the one who says in Yoma (Yoma 4a) that ordination — everything written in them is indispensable; therefore He said <b>and this is the thing</b> — the entire matter stated here is indispensable. And according to the one who says that a matter that is not indispensable for generations is not indispensable in ordination, its saying <b>the thing</b> comes to say: and not every matter is indispensable." "<b>Take a bull, etc.</b> Perhaps permission is given to bring it either from that of Aaron and his sons or from that of Moses, and there is no hindrance in the matter."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:24.822151583Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}